 8.3, "incumbency": -2.0, "money": -1.14}, "rating_margin": -12.5, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.16, "baseline_margin": -8.64, "analyst_adjustment": -1.36, "key_factors": ["R+8 district with Republican incumbent Abraham Hamadeh seeking re-election", "All ten expert ratings favor Republicans; five call it Solid or Safe R", "Hamadeh's fundraising edge: $1.2M raised versus $209K for Greene-Placentia", "Polymarket gives Democrats about a 15% chance; no public general-election polls"], "rationale": "A strongly Republican-leaning district, an incumbent with a roughly five-to-one fundraising advantage, and unanimous expert ratings pointing to a comfortable Republican hold outweigh the underfunded, low-profile challenge; prediction markets still assign Democrats a modest chance, keeping this short of Safe.", "watch": "With no public polling, a late scandal, a surge of outside spending, or a shift in the national environment could move the race quickly.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Abraham Hamadeh (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Arizona's 8th District leans firmly Republican, and first-term incumbent Abraham Hamadeh is seeking re-election with the advantages that come with it. He has raised about $1.2 million and holds a cash edge over Democrat Bernadette Greene-Placentia, a former trucker who won her party's nomination in July and has raised roughly $209,000. No public general-election polls are available for the race.\n\nExpert raters uniformly place the seat in Republican hands: five call it Solid or Safe Republican and five call it Likely Republican. Prediction markets give Democrats roughly a 15 percent chance. Headlines have been mostly routine, including constituent protests over closed-door events alongside Hamadeh's legislative and constituent-service activity, without a major scandal. The district's lean and the incumbent's resources point to a Republican hold, with the main uncertainty being the absence of polling to confirm the margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0839, "margin": -8.56}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0923, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0824, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1327, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0645, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0823, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0978, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0775, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1109, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0711, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0764, "margin": -10.0}]}